{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1528792-how-does-mortal-have-supernatural-power","id":1528792,"title":"How does Mortal have Supernatural Power?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-18T05:57:46-08:00","id":1528792,"title":"How does Mortal have Supernatural Power?","content":"What is the lore behide Mortal having Supernatural Power? Like how did a normal human have Supernatural Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-18T06:19:45-08:00","id":1528793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1528792-how-does-mortal-have-supernatural-power#post1528792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the lore behide Mortal having Supernatural Power? Like how did a normal human have Supernatural Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't any really. They're mostly generic powers that you can skin as you like.<br /> <br /> I guess a lot of them use 'psychic' as a descriptor. Though whether you take that as an explanation or a descriptor is up to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T02:17:15-08:00","id":1528881,"title":"","content":"You're not really a 'normal mortal' anymore once you have a supernatural power... Right? That is a Doylist question of them still using the mortal (base) template.<br /> <br /> From an in-Universe perspective maybe their soul is just a little bit different, like take the Aura reading merit (CofD 56?) Maybe they are more attuned to reading auras because their soul (like mages who twist their souls into legacies, or Devients whose souls are fundamentally broken) is a little non-stansard.<br /> <br /> But then, maybe that explaination wouldn't work for other merits.<br /> <br /> Bless Amulet (HL 72) has prerequisite dots in Occult, so maybe it is more down to knowledge of specific (occult) practices which hold power.<br /> <br /> I imagine every merit could have some alternative (Watsonian) explaination.<br /> <br /> See other merits here: <a href=\"https://codexofdarkness.com/wiki/Merits,_Mortal\" target=\"_blank\">https://codexofdarkness.com/wiki/Merits,_Mortal</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T07:06:42-08:00","id":1528918,"title":"","content":"A lot of the merits are based off things that people claim to be able to do in this world. The justifications can be as much, or as little, as they are in this world, from favored by a god to maybe she's born with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-20T05:03:08-08:00","id":1528994,"title":"","content":"Consider that, from a Mage point of view, even a normal soul is a very potent thing.<br /> Normal mages cannot create souls, and they can burn them to gain a powerful bonus.<br /> In Mage mythology before the Fall of Atlantis probably almost all humans coul do marvels, even if not mages.<br /> The Exarcs uses the Lie to put human souls power to sleep, so you could say that a human with an internal supernatural merit is a little awake about the full potential of his soul.<br /> Human with an external supernatural merit instead, knows a little about the supernatural rules built in the mundane world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}